Internal Audit of ISMS Against ISO 27001:2022
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Set up a working directory structure and scripting tools for ISMS audit documentation
Develop an internal audit plan, defining scope, objectives, and criteria based on ISO 27001:2022 Annex A controls
Simulate evidence collection through scripted checks, interview logs, and walkthrough notes
Record and classify nonconformities (major/minor) and improvement opportunities
Generate a structured internal audit report with a corrective action plan (CAP)
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command-line familiarity (file/directory operations, text editors)
Understanding of ISO 27001:2022 structure (clauses 4-10, Annex A controls)
Familiarity with audit concepts: scope, criteria, evidence, nonconformity (CGRC Domain 5 basics)
No prior scripting expertise required, but basic Bash/Python reading ability helps
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Linux machine (Ubuntu-based) via Start Lab
All work is done locally; no cloud accounts or external services required
Verify environment:

lsb_release -a
python3 --version
which git nano
Install helper tools if missing:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3-pip tree pandoc git
pip3 install --user pandas tabulate
